  partName: Engine Block
  description: The Engine Block, situated at the middle-center-rear of the Hover
    Engine, is a large and complex-shaped component that houses the engine's cylinders,
    pistons, and crankshaft. Made of standardSurface2 material, it provides a strong
    and durable foundation for the engine's operation. Notably, the Engine Block's
    design and material selection play a critical role in maintaining the engine's
    structural integrity and thermal management.
